  <div class="dp-main">

    <!-- §1 Overview -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="overview">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§1</div>
        <h2>Operational Separation</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Every operator session is bound to an <b>environment</b> chosen at login and
        confirmed by the server. The environment determines the signing-key profile,
        whether multi-factor authentication is required, how strictly limits and
        scopes are enforced, and — critically — whether real Real-Time Gross
        Settlement (RTGS) and mainnet currency movements are executed or simulated.</p>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-info"><span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span><div>
        The client never dictates its own permissions. On login the server returns a
        signed session with the operator's granted <b>scopes</b> and the environment
        <b>policy</b>; the desktop app consumes them but can never widen them.
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §2 Environment Model -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="environments">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§2</div>
        <h2>Environment Model — Sandbox vs Production</h2>
      </div>
      <table class="dp-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Feature / Domain</th><th>Sandbox (Training) / Pilot</th><th>Production</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><b>RTGS &amp; Mainnet Hooks</b></td>
            <td><b>Simulated.</b> Calls are suppressed on both client and server. Notes burn, but RTGS credits are dropped.</td>
            <td><b>Live.</b> Executes real RTGS hooks and mainnet currency movements.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><b>Authentication &amp; MFA</b></td>
            <td><b>Optional OTP.</b> TOTP is not enforced during sign-in.</td>
            <td><b>Mandatory TOTP.</b> Cryptographically verifies a 6-digit TOTP / YubiKey code on login.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><b>Key Profile &amp; Scopes</b></td>
            <td>Sandbox/staging key profiles with server-granted scopes for safe functional testing.</td>
            <td>Production key profile with server-enforced RBAC scope grants.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><b>Data &amp; State Impact</b></td>
            <td>Isolated test state; safe for demo burns and training runs.</td>
            <td>Direct monetary, compliance, and ledger impact across live accounts.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>The three environments and their policy (single source of truth in
        <code>RbacPolicy::ENV_POLICY</code>, mirrored by the client
        <code>SessionManager::EnvironmentPolicy</code>):</p>
      <table class="dp-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Environment</th><th>key_profile</th><th>mfa_required</th><th>strict</th><th>rtgs_live</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Training / Sandbox</td><td>simulated</td><td>no</td><td>no</td><td>no</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Pilot / Staging</td><td>staging</td><td>no</td><td>yes</td><td>no</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Production</td><td>production</td><td><b>yes</b></td><td>yes</td><td><b>yes</b></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-info"><span class="dp-ci">ℹ</span><div>
        An unknown or missing environment resolves to <b>Sandbox</b> (least privilege).
        The desktop client's login environment selector <b>defaults to Sandbox</b>
        when nothing valid is saved — it never defaults to Production, so an operator
        can't enter a LIVE session just by accepting the first item.
      </div></div>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-warn"><span class="dp-ci">⚠</span><div>
        <b>"Sandbox" is a policy posture, not a separate database.</b> The client always
        talks to the same backend/database; the environment does not switch data stores.
        What isolates a sandbox session is <code>rtgs_live=false</code> (plus
        <code>strict=false</code> and simulated signing keys) — it <b>suppresses the real
        RTGS / mainnet settlement hooks</b>, so notes still move logically but no live
        money movement occurs. Isolation is the <code>rtgs_live</code> flag, not a DB
        boundary; a physically separate sandbox database would be a distinct
        infrastructure change.
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §3 RBAC -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="rbac">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§3</div>
        <h2>Role-Based Access Control &amp; Scopes</h2>
      </div>
      <p>On login the server returns the operator's <b>scopes</b> for the active
        environment. The desktop client hides tabs and disables action buttons the
        operator's scopes do not cover — <code>governor</code> receives every scope,
        <code>system_admin</code> the <code>*</code> wildcard.</p>
      <table class="dp-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Role</th><th>Granted scopes (summary)</th><th>Visible tabs</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Minting Officer</td><td>issuance.authorize, issuance.mint, issuance.burn, audit.read</td><td>Issuance, Deposit &amp; Burn, Audit</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Forensic Auditor</td><td>audit.read, system_events.read, fraud.review</td><td>Audit, System Events, Fraud</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Compliance Officer</td><td>validation.*, corridor.execute, quarantine.manage, fraud.review, audit.read</td><td>Validation, Corridor Ops, Quarantine, Fraud, Audit</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Corridor Operator</td><td>corridor.execute, gateway.manage, audit.read</td><td>Corridor Ops, Regional Gateways, Audit</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Governor</td><td>all scopes (incl. governance.clearance)</td><td>all</td></tr>
          <tr><td>System Admin</td><td><code>*</code> (unrestricted)</td><td>all</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Commercial Institution&nbsp;Operator</td><td><code>claim.create</code>, <code>claim.read</code> (only)</td><td>Trade Claim / Counterparty Portal only</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Key action buttons — Authorize, Mint, Burn, Governance Clearance — are
        gated by the corresponding scope (<code>issuance.authorize</code>,
        <code>issuance.mint</code>, <code>issuance.burn</code>,
        <code>governance.clearance</code>).</p>
      <p><b>Segregation of Duties.</b> The six roles above are central-bank node /
        platform operators. <b>Commercial Institution Operator</b> is the only
        dealer-bank (maker) role: it may <b>only</b> create trade claims and read the
        lifecycle of its <b>own institution's</b> claims. With no sovereign scopes,
        <code>can_mint?</code> and supervisor-capability both fail, hard-blocking
        Issuance, Supervisor Desk, Deposit &amp; Burn, Corridor Ops, Validation Desk,
        and Governance. Its trade-claim list is enclosed to
        <code>submitted_by_institution_swift</code> — it can never see other
        counterparties' or central-bank claims. Provision it in
        <code>/admin/operator_accounts</code>.</p>
      <p><b>Sovereign jurisdiction locks.</b> Two write-time boundaries reinforce the
        model: the <b>Governor Console</b> only halts/injects/adjusts corridors whose
        origin OR destination is the governor's home country (server-enforced by
        <code>SovereignOriginGuard</code> → 403 <code>sovereign_jurisdiction_violation</code>);
        and the <b>Minting Desk</b> SELECT SOURCE strictly scopes to authorizations
        whose corridor <b>targets</b> the operator's home country, so only the
        destination central bank can mint a destination liability (e.g. only CBN/NGA
        may mint an L-NGN note from a GHA→NGA claim). <code>system_admin</code> bypasses.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- §4 MFA -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="mfa">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§4</div>
        <h2>Multi-Factor Authentication (TOTP)</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Production logins require a valid <b>RFC 6238 TOTP</b> code (authenticator
        app or YubiKey-TOTP). The server verifies the 6-digit code against the
        operator's enrolled secret; an un-enrolled operator cannot sign in to
        Production. Pilot and Sandbox remain MFA-optional.</p>

      <figure style="margin: 1.25rem 0 1.75rem; text-align: center;">
        <img src="/docs/operator-login-mfa.png"
             alt="bearerCORE Secure Operator Authentication screen — Operator ID and passphrase fields, a green 'SECURITY TOKEN / OTP — REQUIRED' field, and an Environment selector open on Production / Pilot · Staging / Training · Sandbox"
             style="width: 100%; max-width: 640px; height: auto; border: 1px solid #d7dce3; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 2px 10px rgba(16,24,40,.08);"
             loading="lazy">
        <figcaption style="margin-top: .5rem; font-size: 12px; color: #6c757d;">
          The Secure Operator Authentication screen. With <strong>Production</strong> selected the
          OTP header turns green <strong>REQUIRED</strong> and the field is enforced pre-flight; the
          <strong>Environment</strong> selector binds the session to Production, Pilot / Staging, or
          Training / Sandbox.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <ul class="dp-list">
        <li>TOTP secrets are <b>encrypted at rest</b> via ActiveRecord Encryption.</li>
        <li>Enrolment is admin-controlled: <code>rake "otp:provision[username]"</code> issues an <code>otpauth://</code> URI to scan; <code>otp:status</code> and <code>otp:revoke[username]</code> manage it.</li>
        <li>The login screen's OTP header turns <span style="color:#1b5e20;font-weight:700;">green "REQUIRED"</span> when Production is selected and stays muted/optional otherwise.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-warn"><span class="dp-ci">⚠</span><div>
        Every operator who signs in to Production must be enrolled before MFA is
        enforced — an un-enrolled account is locked out of Production.
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §5 RTGS -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="rtgs">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§5</div>
        <h2>RTGS &amp; Settlement Isolation</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Only Production fires live settlement. In Sandbox/Pilot the note still burns,
        but the RTGS credit is <b>suppressed</b> — enforced twice:</p>
      <ul class="dp-list">
        <li><b>Client:</b> the burn confirmation states
          <code>⚠ Training/Sandbox — settlement SIMULATED, no live RTGS credit</code>,
          and the request payload carries <code>environment</code> and
          <code>rtgs_live: false</code>.</li>
        <li><b>Server:</b> the burn endpoint honours <code>rtgs_live</code> — when
          false it records the burn without crediting RTGS (drops the account).</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-danger"><span class="dp-ci">●</span><div>
        In Production, burns credit RTGS and produce direct monetary, compliance,
        and ledger impact. A red <b>PRODUCTION — LIVE</b> banner is shown across the
        top of the app to signal this at all times.
      </div></div>
    </div>

    <!-- §6 Enforcement -->
    <div class="dp-section" id="enforcement">
      <div class="dp-section-header">
        <div class="dp-section-num">§6</div>
        <h2>Enforcement &amp; UI Signals</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Defence-in-depth: the server is authoritative, and the client enforces the
        same posture locally so violations never reach the wire.</p>
      <table class="dp-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Signal / Control</th><th>Behaviour</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Environment banner</td><td>Amber "TRAINING / SANDBOX" or "PILOT / STAGING" for isolated modes; red "PRODUCTION — LIVE" for real settlement. Always visible.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>OTP field header</td><td>Muted "optional" for Pilot/Sandbox; green "REQUIRED" for Production, with a pre-flight check.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tab &amp; button gating</td><td>Tabs hidden and action buttons disabled by <code>hasScope()</code> against server-granted scopes.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Burn safeguard</td><td>Simulated-settlement warning + <code>rtgs_live</code> stamp in Sandbox/Pilot.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="dp-callout dp-ok"><span class="dp-ci">✓</span><div>
        Server API: <code>POST /api/v2/auth/login</code> returns
        <code>{ role, token, environment, key_profile, policy, scopes }</code>.
        The client's <code>SessionManager</code> captures these and applies the
        environment policy + scope gating on session start.
      </div></div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
